---

Data provenance (applies to files under `data/`):

- `australia-surf-breaks-enriched.json` — spot records partly generated with
  NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning (open weights); `state` / `region` / base
  location fields come from a human-curated input list.
- Break coordinates are maintained against OpenStreetMap data
  (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/).
- `climate/*.json` — 5-year ERA5 swell profiles (Copernicus / ECMWF
  reanalysis); ERA5 data is redistributed under the Copernicus Licence —
  no restriction on redistribution, attribution required.
- Seafloor / bathymetry fetched at run time from GEBCO (public domain).
- Forecast data fetched at run time from Open-Meteo (free for non-commercial
  use, attribution "Open-Meteo.com" required — see
  https://open-meteo.com/terms-of-service).

Where redistribution of a third-party dataset is concerned, its own terms
apply on top of the MIT licence above.